Not upstream (no QTBUG, unchanged on qtbase dev as of 2026-11). Drop this patch when moving
to a Qt release whose -[QIOSViewController updatePlatformScreen] compares the scene role
with isEqualToString:.
Subject: [PATCH] iOS: Compare the scene session role by value

updatePlatformScreen compared windowScene.session.role with
UIWindowSceneSessionRoleApplication using ==, which compares the NSString
pointers. On iPadOS 27 the session returns a copy of the string, so
isPrimaryScene was false: the screen of the scene never became the primary
QScreen and existing windows were not adopted. In windowed mode with a window
smaller than the display, the scene is on its own UIScreen, so windows created
later went to the main screen, which has no scene, and the app stayed black.

--- a/src/plugins/platforms/ios/qiosviewcontroller.mm
+++ b/src/plugins/platforms/ios/qiosviewcontroller.mm
@@ -341,7 +341,7 @@
         QScreen *newScreen = newPlatformScreen ? newPlatformScreen->screen() : nullptr;
 
         const bool isPrimaryScene = !qt_apple_sharedApplication().supportsMultipleScenes
-            && windowScene.session.role == UIWindowSceneSessionRoleApplication;
+            && [windowScene.session.role isEqualToString:UIWindowSceneSessionRoleApplication];
 
         if (isPrimaryScene) {
             // When we only have a single application-role scene we treat the
